The artifacts built here contain:

- sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx) - Apache-2.0
- ONNX Runtime (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime) - MIT
- kaldi-native-fbank (https://github.com/csukuangfj/kaldi-native-fbank) - Apache-2.0
- kaldi-decoder (https://github.com/k2-fsa/kaldi-decoder) - Apache-2.0
- kaldifst (https://github.com/k2-fsa/kaldifst) - Apache-2.0
- KISS FFT (https://github.com/mborgerding/kissfft) - BSD-3-Clause
- OpenFst (https://www.openfst.org) - Apache-2.0
- simple-sentencepiece (https://github.com/pkufool/simple-sentencepiece) - Apache-2.0
- Eigen (https://eigen.tuxfamily.org) - MPL-2.0 (unmodified)
- nlohmann/json (https://github.com/nlohmann/json) - MIT
- hclust-cpp (https://github.com/cdalitz/hclust-cpp) - BSD-3-Clause

They do NOT contain espeak-ng or piper-phonemize: sherpa-onnx is built
with SHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=OFF, and the build fails if any native
library contains espeak-ng code.
